---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base title="Terms of use" description="The terms for using Open World Life, including exploring safely.">
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {site.policiesUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      These terms apply to your use of the {site.name} app and this website, which are provided by {site.publisher}{' '}
      (“we”). By using the app you agree to them. If you got the app from Apple’s App Store, Apple’s{' '}
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/">Standard End User License Agreement</a>{' '}
      also applies; if you got it from Google Play, Google Play’s terms also apply.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Explore safely</h2>
    <div class="callout">
      The app is a game, not a navigation or safety tool. Your safety is your responsibility.
    </div>
    <ul>
      <li>Pay attention to your surroundings, not your screen.</li>
      <li>Don’t use the app while driving or cycling. If you’re in a vehicle, let a passenger handle the phone.</li>
      <li>
        Unlocking the map is never a reason to go somewhere you shouldn’t. Respect private property, closures, local laws
        and the rules of parks and protected areas.
      </li>
      <li>
        In the backcountry, carry proper navigation and safety equipment, check the conditions, and tell someone your
        plans. Don’t rely on the app or your phone’s battery.
      </li>
      <li>
        Map data, boundaries and water areas come from OpenStreetMap and may be incomplete, inaccurate or out of date.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Your licence to use the app</h2>
    <p>
      When you buy the app, you get a personal, non-transferable licence to use it on devices you own or control, under
      the rules of the store you bought it from. Please don’t copy, resell, reverse engineer or misuse the app or the
      services it relies on, except where the law allows it.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Purchases and refunds</h2>
    <p>
      The app is sold through the App Store and Google Play. Payments and refunds are handled by Apple or Google under
      their policies; we can’t process refunds ourselves.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Your data</h2>
    <p>
      Your location and progress stay on your phone. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for details. You’re
      responsible for your phone’s backups; if progress is lost with a phone that wasn’t backed up, we can’t recover it.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Map data and third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Map data is © <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap contributors</a>, available under the
      Open Database License. Map tiles are provided by <a href="https://openfreemap.org">OpenFreeMap</a>. These services
      are run by third parties and may change or be unavailable at times.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Changes to the app</h2>
    <p>We may update, change or discontinue features of the app from time to time.</p>

    <h2>7. No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The app is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, including that it will be accurate,
      uninterrupted or error-free, to the extent the law allows.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental or consequential damages, or for any
      injury, loss or damage arising from your activities while using the app. Our total liability is limited to the
      amount you paid for the app. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under consumer protection laws that
      can’t be limited.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>If these terms change, we’ll update this page and the date above. Continuing to use the app means you accept them.</p>

    <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of {site.governingLaw}, except where your local law says otherwise.</p>

    <h2>11. Contact</h2>
    <p>{site.publisher}, <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
